  "notes": "Volvo AU's own EX30/EX90 spec pages label the consumption figure as 'NEDC' even though Volvo AU markets its range figures elsewhere as WLTP; this looks like a site labelling artefact rather than a genuine NEDC test, so rangeCycle is recorded as null for EX30/EX90 rather than guessed. The dedicated EC40 specifications sub-page returned 404 at fetch time, so EC40 numeric specs (battery, power, range) could not be confirmed from the primary source; only a price figure from a secondary source (CarsGuide) is included, flagged low-confidence. Community-sourced ev-wiki.org mentions of an 'ES90' for Volvo Australia was NOT corroborated by any official or reputable press source and has been excluded entirely rather than included as a speculative row. EX40 (the renamed XC40 Recharge — previously wrongly excluded from this file as an unconfirmed 'community-sourced' claim; it is in fact a genuine, currently-sold model) has now been added. Its /specifications/ sub-page returned 403 at fetch time, so EX40 figures below are press-sourced (CarExpert, thebeep) rather than manufacturer-confirmed, and are flagged low-confidence accordingly. Press sources disagreed materially on price by ~$5,000-13,000 depending on state/promo/drive-away timing; the figures used here come from CarExpert's 2026-03-31 report of a $7,000 national MSRP price cut, which is the most specific and recent single data point found. PRICE AND SPEC CORRECTIONS (Sept 2026 pass): volvocars.com.au's own /specifications/ pages for EX30 and EX90 return 403 to automated fetches (Volvo's own bot-blocking, not a client-side network/VPN issue — confirmed by retrying after ruling out a local Cloudflare WARP/DNS cause), so this pass is press-sourced. EX30 priceAud filled from CarExpert's dedicated Plus/Ultra spec pages and its EX30 Cross Country pricing article, which gives a clean one-page table of all four current EX30 configurations. EX90 priceAud filled from a Chasing Cars review giving both Plus ($124,990) and Ultra Performance ($134,990) prices with matching power/torque figures. While researching EX90 pricing, multiple independent sources (CarsGuide's own Plus Twin Motor spec page, thebeep.com.au, Chasing Cars, general press) consistently gave power/torque/range/0-100 figures materially different from what this file previously recorded (300kW/770Nm/5.9s for Twin Motor vs the previous 330kW/670Nm/5.5s; 380kW/910Nm/4.9s for Twin Motor Performance vs the previous 500kW/870Nm/4.2s; 570km WLTP for both vs the previous 521km) — these look like a genuine prior data error rather than a source disagreement, since every current source agrees with each other and disagrees with the old figures, so they have been corrected rather than left as a documented conflict. EX30's existing power/torque/battery/range figures were re-checked against CarExpert's dedicated Plus/Ultra spec pages during this pass and found to match exactly (200kW/343Nm/69kWh gross/64kWh usable/462km WLTP for Single Motor Extended Range), so those fields were left unchanged.",
